*> The world clock of the time command (docs/protocol/16-commands-catalog.md §4.5, §13 advance_time). The state is the clock of the world
*> simulation (core/copy/WSIM2.cpy: W2-PAUSED, W2-RATE, W2-ADVANCE; the tick is WORLDSIM-CLOCK-STEP).
*>
*> Entry points:
*>   BR-CLOCK-STATE USING paused out, rate out (FLOAT-LONG): the state after making it ready
*>   BR-CLOCK-SET USING paused (BINARY-LONG), rate (FLOAT-LONG): the state (pause, resume and rate of the time command)
*>   BR-SEND-TIME: Set Time (with the clock's rate) to every player whose join has been sent

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. BR-CLOCK-STATE.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY WSIM2.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-PAUSED               BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-RATE                 FLOAT-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-PAUSED L-RATE.
     CALL "WORLDSIM-ENSURE2"
     MOVE W2-PAUSED TO L-PAUSED
     MOVE W2-RATE TO L-RATE
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM BR-CLOCK-STATE.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. BR-CLOCK-SET.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY WSIM2.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-PAUSED               BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-RATE                 FLOAT-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-PAUSED L-RATE.
     CALL "WORLDSIM-ENSURE2"
     MOVE L-PAUSED TO W2-PAUSED
     MOVE L-RATE TO W2-RATE
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM BR-CLOCK-SET.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. BR-SEND-TIME.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CORESTATE.
 COPY PROTO.
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 64.
 01 WS-ROW                 BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "PB-INIT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
     CALL "PLAY-TIME-RATE-BUILD" USING CW-TIME PB-BUFFER
     PERFORM VARYING WS-ROW FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-ROW > CORE-MAX-PLAYERS
         IF PL-USED(WS-ROW) = 1 AND PL-ENTITY-ROW(WS-ROW) > 0
             CALL "CORE-SEND" USING PL-CONN(WS-ROW) PB-BUFFER
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM
     CALL "PB-FREE" USING PB-BUFFER
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM BR-SEND-TIME.
